1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,500
LabWeaver links materials, approvals, environments, access, resources, and evidence into one traceable journey.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:19,500
Six domain services coordinate through PostgreSQL authoritative state and NATS JetStream events.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,500
Container and KubeVirt VM share one contract while dedicated executors isolate runtime failures.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,500
The teacher uploads public-safe material and checks LLM egress and protected-content boundaries.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,500
AgentRuns create Environment and Evaluation candidates; deterministic tools validate them before execution.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,500
The teacher independently reviews candidate differences, validation results, and reasons.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:01:14,500
Immutable releases retain source, validation result, and Runtime identity to prevent silent drift.

8
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:15,500
The administrator handles a resource request produced by the formal Work/Agent path.

9
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,500
Scope review, an explicit reason, and confirmation make the resource decision accountable.

10
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:39,500
ResourceQuota and time-bounded Lease readback give capacity allocation an explicit scope and lifetime.

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:40,500
The student creates a Container from a teacher-published template under Environment Service lifecycle ownership.

12
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:41,500
An AccessGrant binds role, endpoint, and expiry after the environment becomes ready.

13
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:42,500
Only a valid ConsoleCapability opens the browser xterm.

14
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,500
The student edits, compiles, and runs the public C++ sample with material and release identity intact.

15
00:01:47,000 --> 00:02:29,500
Resize, disconnect, and reconnect return to the same environment while lifecycle remains tracked.

16
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:30,500
The KubeVirt Provider brings Linux labs under the same Environment contract as Container labs.

17
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:31,500
AccessGrant and ConsoleCapability jointly constrain VM console access.

18
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,500
Short-lived authorization becomes controlled noVNC access without directly exposing VMI endpoints.

19
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,500
A dedicated executor reconciles stop/start or recovery and preserves environment identity.

20
00:02:40,000 --> 00:03:24,500
This rehearsal keeps its Fixture boundary; real VMI/noVNC success remains with #126 connected acceptance.

21
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,500
Freezing first loads the same environment and grant so another runtime instance cannot be mixed in.

22
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:49,500
Object Version, SHA-256, source commit, and runtime identity form one auditable evidence chain.

23
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:50,500
The student must obtain an AccessGrant bound to role, endpoint, and expiry.

24
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:51,500
The console session remains tied to the grant revision instead of checking only at connection time.

25
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:14,500
Revocation closes the session and a reconnect receives a stable fail-closed diagnostic.

26
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:15,500
Cleanup binds an explicit Environment identity to avoid deleting another environment.

27
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,500
Explicit confirmation triggers the controlled lifecycle transition and runtime reclamation.

28
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:29,500
Readback returns a stable not-found diagnostic and closes the evidence and resource lifecycle.
